const e={id:"js-error-handling",title:{en:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors"},difficulty:"Beginner",readTime:8,sections:[{type:"concept",heading:{en:"1. What is Error Handling in JavaScript?",hi:"1. JavaScript Mein Error Handling Kya Hai?"},body:{en:"Errors in JavaScript are runtime events that disrupt the normal flow of program execution. If an unhandled exception occurs, the JavaScript engine halts execution immediately, crashing the running script or server process!\n\nTo handle failures gracefully, JavaScript provides the **`try...catch...finally`** construct:\n- **`try` block**: Encloses the risky code that might throw an error (e.g., parsing JSON, reading a file, network operations).\n- **`catch (error)` block**: Executes *only* if an exception is thrown inside the `try` block. It receives the error object containing details about what went wrong.\n- **`finally` block**: Executes **always**, regardless of whether an error was thrown or caught. Ideal for cleanup actions like closing database connections or clearing loading spinners.\n\n### Anatomy of an Error Object\nJavaScript's built-in `Error` object provides 3 key properties:\n1. `error.name`: The type of error (e.g., `TypeError`, `ReferenceError`, `SyntaxError`).\n2. `error.message`: A human-readable text explanation of the issue.\n3. `error.stack`: The full stack trace showing the exact file and line numbers where the error originated.",hi:"JavaScript mein Error ek aisi runtime event hai jo code ke normal flow ko rok deti hai. Agar kisi error ko handle na kiya jaye (unhandled exception), toh poora program ya server crash ho jata hai!\n\nProgram ko crash hone se bachane ke liye JavaScript humein **`try...catch...finally`** blocks deta hai:\n- **`try` block**: Wo code jahan galti hone ka risk ho (jaise network call, JSON parsing ya file read).\n- **`catch (error)` block**: Yeh block tabhi chalta hai jab `try` ke andar koi exception throw hoti hai. Isme error object milta hai jisse hum problem ko inspect kar sakte hain.\n- **`finally` block**: Yeh **hamesha execute hota hai**, chahe error aaye ya na aaye. Loading spinner band karne ya database connection close karne ke liye best hai.\n\n### Error Object Ke 3 Mukhya Hissay\n1. `error.name`: Error ka type (jaise `TypeError`, `ReferenceError`).\n2. `error.message`: Galti ka description string.\n3. `error.stack`: File name aur exact line number ka trace jahan error generate hui."}},{type:"concept",heading:{en:"2. Why Structured Error Handling Matters",hi:"2. Proper Error Handling Kyun Zaroori Hai?"},body:{en:`In a production MERN application:
1. **Prevents Server Downtime**: In Node.js, an uncaught exception crashes the entire Express server process, knocking every user offline!
2. **Superior User Experience (UX)**: Instead of a blank white screen, users see actionable notifications ("Payment failed: card expired").
3. **Security**: Proper error handlers mask sensitive internal database credentials and raw SQL/Mongoose errors from external attackers.
4. **Debugging Velocity**: Rich error messages and stack traces allow teams to diagnose production bugs in seconds using monitoring tools (like Sentry or Datadog).`,hi:`Production MERN apps mein error handling sabse zaroori pillar hai:
1. **Server Ko Crash Hone Se Bachana**: Node.js mein unhandled error aate hi poora Express server shutdown ho jata hai aur sabhi users disconnect ho jaate hain!
2. **Better User Experience**: White screen of death ki jagah user ko clear message milta hai ("Mobile number invalid hai").
3. **Security**: Proper error handling se database connection strings aur server paths hackers ke saamne expose hone se bachte hain.
4. **Fast Debugging**: Error logs dekhkar developer ko pata chal jata hai ki bug kis file ke kis line number pe hai.`}},{type:"analogy",heading:{en:"Real-Life Analogy: The Indian Railways Emergency Chain",hi:"Real-Life Analogy: Indian Railways Ki Emergency Chain"},body:{en:"Consider traveling on an **Indian Railways Express Train**:\n\n- **Normal Flow (`try` block)**: The train travels smoothly at 130 km/h towards New Delhi.\n- **Unexpected Hazard (`throw new Error()`)**: A passenger spots smoke in compartment B-4.\n- **The Emergency Chain (`catch` block)**: The passenger pulls the red alarm chain. The train brakes smoothly to a controlled halt, alerts the train guard, and notifies station control with the exact coach number (Stack Trace) instead of crashing the entire train!\n- **Inspection & Clean-Up (`finally` block)**: Whether it was a genuine fire or a false alarm, the railway staff inspects the track, resets the pressure valve, and ensures the signal is green before the journey resumes.",hi:"Sochiye **Indian Railways** ki train safar:\n\n- **Normal Flow (`try` block)**: Train 130 km/h ki speed se bina kisi rukawat ke chal rahi hai.\n- **Problem Spotting (`throw new Error()`)**: Coach B-4 mein smoke detect hota hai.\n- **Emergency Chain (`catch` block)**: Passenger ne red chain kheenchi. Train derailing se bach gayi, brakes safe tareeke se lage aur guard ko pata chal gaya ki dikkat coach B-4 mein hai.\n- **Cleanup (`finally` block)**: Chahe false alarm ho ya real problem, inspection team coach check karegi, air pressure reset karegi aur train aage badhegi."}},{type:"syntax",heading:{en:"4. Syntax: try...catch...finally & Custom Error Classes",hi:"4. Syntax: try...catch...finally Aur Custom Errors"},body:{en:`### Basic Pattern
\`\`\`javascript
try {
  // Risky code
  throw new Error("Something went wrong!");
} catch (err) {
  // Handle failure
  console.error(err.name, err.message);
} finally {
  // Runs in ALL circumstances
  console.log("Cleanup executed.");
}
\`\`\`

### Creating Custom Application Errors
In modern JavaScript and Express.js, standard practice is to extend the built-in \`Error\` class to include HTTP status codes and operational flags.`,hi:`### Basic Try Catch Structure
\`\`\`javascript
try {
  // Jo code fail ho sakta hai
  throw new Error("Payment fail ho gaya!");
} catch (err) {
  // Error ko pakdo aur handle karo
  console.error(err.name, err.message);
} finally {
  // Har haal mein chalega
  console.log("Cleanup complete.");
}
\`\`\`

### Custom Error Class Banana
Express.js backend mein hum built-in \`Error\` class ko extend karke custom error banate hain jismein HTTP status codes (400, 404, 500) attach hote hain.`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"5. Practical Examples: Safe JSON Parsing, Custom Errors, and Async Handlers",hi:"5. Practical Examples: Safe JSON Parsing, Custom Errors, aur Async Handlers"},body:{en:"### Example 1: Safe JSON Parsing with try...catch...finally\n`JSON.parse()` throws a fatal `SyntaxError` if given malformed input. This utility ensures application stability.",hi:`### Example 1: Safe JSON Parser Utility
Malformed JSON milne par app crash hone se bachane ka safe tareeka.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"safeJsonParse.js",snippet:`// Example 1: Safe JSON Parser with Fallback
function safeJsonParse(jsonString, fallbackValue = {}) {
  let isSuccessful = false;

  try {
    const parsedData = JSON.parse(jsonString);
    isSuccessful = true;
    return parsedData;
  } catch (error) {
    console.warn(\`[JSON Parse Error]: Invalid JSON detected. Details: \${error.message}\`);
    return fallbackValue;
  } finally {
    console.log(\`Parse attempt completed. Status: \${isSuccessful ? "SUCCESS" : "FALLBACK_USED"}\`);
  }
}

// Valid JSON
const user = safeJsonParse('{"name": "Aditya", "role": "FullStack"}');
console.log("Parsed User:", user);

// Malformed invalid JSON (missing quotes)
const badData = safeJsonParse('{name: Aditya}');
console.log("Fallback result:", badData); // Returns {} instead of crashing!`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 2: Custom Error Hierarchy for MERN Backend",hi:"Example 2: Express Backend Ke Liye Custom Error Classes"},body:{en:`### Example 2: Enterprise Custom Error Classes
Distinguishing between Client Validation Errors (400), Not Found Errors (404), and Internal Server Errors (500).`,hi:`### Example 2: Custom Application Error Classes
Client errors (400, 404) aur internal server errors ko alag classify karne ke liye custom classes.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"customErrors.js",snippet:`// Example 2: Custom Application Error Hierarchy
class AppError extends Error {
  constructor(message, statusCode) {
    super(message);
    this.statusCode = statusCode;
    this.status = \`\${statusCode}\`.startsWith("4") ? "fail" : "error";
    this.isOperational = true; // Flag for predictable bugs vs system crashes

    Error.captureStackTrace(this, this.constructor);
  }
}

class ValidationError extends AppError {
  constructor(message) {
    super(message, 400);
    this.name = "ValidationError";
  }
}

class NotFoundError extends AppError {
  constructor(resource) {
    super(\`\${resource} was not found on this server.\`, 404);
    this.name = "NotFoundError";
  }
}

// Testing the custom error flow
function findUserById(id) {
  if (typeof id !== "number") {
    throw new ValidationError("User ID must be a numeric integer!");
  }
  const users = { 1: "Siddharth", 2: "Ananya" };
  if (!users[id]) {
    throw new NotFoundError(\`User with ID \${id}\`);
  }
  return users[id];
}

try {
  findUserById("abc"); // Invalid type
} catch (err) {
  console.log(\`Caught \${err.name} [\${err.statusCode}]: \${err.message}\`);
}

try {
  findUserById(99); // Non-existent user
} catch (err) {
  console.log(\`Caught \${err.name} [\${err.statusCode}]: \${err.message}\`);
}`}},{type:"example",heading:{en:"Example 3: Async Error Handling & Express Wrapper Pattern",hi:"Example 3: Async/Await Error Handling & Async Handler Wrapper"},body:{en:`### Example 3: Handling Errors in Asynchronous Code
How to catch errors in async promises without cluttering controllers with repetitive try/catch blocks.`,hi:`### Example 3: Async Code Mein Errors Handle Karna
Async/await ke saath try/catch lagana aur Express controllers ke liye clean asyncHandler wrapper.`},code:{language:"javascript",filename:"asyncErrorHandling.js",snippet:`// Example 3: Clean Async Error Handling Wrapper
// Standard Express asyncHandler utility
const asyncHandler = (fn) => (req, res, next) => {
  Promise.resolve(fn(req, res, next)).catch(next);
};

// Simulated mock database fetch
const fetchProductFromDB = async (productId) => {
  if (productId === "fail") {
    throw new Error("Database connection timed out after 3000ms");
  }
  return { id: productId, name: "Mechanical Keyboard", price: 3499 };
};

// Async controller with comprehensive error recovery
async function getProductController(productId) {
  let spinnerActive = true;

  try {
    console.log("[Info]: Initiating database query...");
    const product = await fetchProductFromDB(productId);
    console.log("[Success]: Fetched product:", product.name);
    return { success: true, data: product };
  } catch (err) {
    console.error(\`[Controller Error Caught]: \${err.message}\`);
    return { success: false, error: "Unable to retrieve product at this time." };
  } finally {
    spinnerActive = false;
    console.log(\`[Cleanup]: Loading spinner deactivated (\${spinnerActive}).\`);
  }
}

// Running the controller
getProductController("prod_101");
getProductController("fail");`}},{type:"mistakes",heading:{en:"6. Common Mistakes in Error Handling",hi:"6. Error Handling Ki Common Galtiyan"},mistakes:[{mistake:{en:"Silent failure / Empty catch blocks ('swallowing' the error).",hi:"Catch block ko khali chhod dena (Error ko swallow kar lena)."},correction:{en:"Never write an empty `catch(err) {}`. If you suppress errors silently, finding critical production bugs becomes nearly impossible. Always log or rethrow.",hi:"Kabhi bhi khali catch block na banayein. Agar error ko bina log kiye daba denge toh production mein bugs dhoondhna impossible ho jayega."},code:`// DISASTROUS ANTI-PATTERN:
try {
  processPayment();
} catch (e) {
  // Silent swallowed error! User is charged, order never placed!
}

// CORRECT:
try {
  processPayment();
} catch (error) {
  logger.error("Payment processing failed", { error });
  notifyUser("Payment could not be processed. Please try again.");
}`},{mistake:{en:"Throwing plain strings or numbers instead of instances of Error.",hi:"Error instance ki jagah normal string throw karna (`throw 'something went wrong'`)."},correction:{en:"Always throw `new Error('message')`. Throwing raw strings loses the stack trace, making it impossible to determine what line caused the exception.",hi:"Hamesha `new Error()` throw karein taaki stack trace preserve rahe aur file/line number ka pata chal sake."},code:`// BAD:
// throw "Database connection failed"; // No stack trace!

// GOOD:
throw new Error("Database connection failed"); // Captures call stack`}]},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"7. Production Error Handling Best Practices",hi:"7. Production Error Handling Best Practices"},body:{en:"- **Centralized Express Error Middleware**: In your backend, implement a 4-argument error handler `(err, req, res, next)` at the very end of your middleware pipeline.\n- **Fail Fast, Fail Cleanly**: Validate incoming inputs early and throw descriptive `ValidationError` instances before expensive database calls.\n- **Always Clean Up in `finally`**: File descriptors, network sockets, and UI loaders must be cleaned up inside the `finally` block.\n- **Handle Promise Rejections**: Always attach `.catch()` or use `try...catch` with `await` to prevent `UnhandledPromiseRejection` warnings.",hi:"- **Express Global Error Middleware**: Backend mein hamesha 4 arguments wala `(err, req, res, next)` global error handler banayein.\n- **Fail Fast Approach**: Request data ko pehle hi validate karein aur validation error throw karein taaki database par faltu load na pade.\n- **Cleanup Hamesha `finally` Mein**: File band karna ya spinner hatana hamesha `finally` block mein karein.\n- **Promise Rejections Ko Handle Karein**: Har async operation ke saath `try...catch` ya `.catch()` lagayein."}},{type:"interview",heading:{en:"8. Top Interview Questions & Answers",hi:"8. Top Interview Sawal Aur Jawab"},questions:[{q:{en:"Will the code inside a `finally` block execute if the `try` block has a `return` statement?",hi:"Kya `finally` block chalega agar `try` block ke andar `return` statement ho?"},a:{en:"Yes! Even if the `try` block executes a `return` statement, the `finally` block is guaranteed to execute immediately before the function actually returns control to the caller.",hi:"Haan! Agar `try` block ke andar `return` likha ho, tab bhi function return hone se pehle `finally` block 100% execute hota hai."}},{q:{en:"What is the difference between an operational error and a programmer error?",hi:"Operational error aur Programmer error mein kya antar hota hai?"},a:{en:"Operational errors represent expected, unavoidable runtime failures in a working system (e.g., database timeout, invalid user email, network down). Programmer errors are actual software bugs in code (e.g., trying to read property of undefined, syntax error). Operational errors should be caught and handled gracefully, while programmer errors should trigger crash alerts and fixes.",hi:"Operational errors real-world issues hote hain jo code theek hone par bhi aa sakte hain (jaise internet disconnect hona ya wrong password). Programmer errors code ke bugs hote hain (jaise undefined ka property padhna). Operational errors ko gracefully handle karna chahiye jabki programmer errors ko turant fix karna chahiye."}},{q:{en:"Why does `try { setTimeout(() => { throw new Error('Boom'); }, 1000); } catch(e) {}` fail to catch the error?",hi:"`try` block ke andar asynchronous `setTimeout` ka error `catch` kyun nahi pakad pata?"},a:{en:"Because the `try...catch` block executes synchronously and exits immediately. By the time the `setTimeout` callback executes 1000ms later from the Macrotask Queue, the original `try...catch` context has long been removed from the Call Stack. To catch async errors, the callback itself must contain its own `try...catch` or return a Promise handled with `.catch()` / `await`.",hi:"Kyunki `try...catch` synchronously execute hoke call stack se hat jata hai. 1000ms baad jab `setTimeout` ka callback event queue se stack par aata hai, tab `try...catch` wahan maujood hi nahi hota. Asynchronous code ko handle karne ke liye callback ke andar `try...catch` lagana padta hai ya async/await use karna padta hai."}}]},{type:"summary",heading:{en:"9. Summary Cheatsheet",hi:"9. Summary Cheatsheet"},body:{en:"- **try**: Enclose code that might fail.\n- **catch(err)**: Intercept failure; access `err.name`, `err.message`, `err.stack`.\n- **finally**: Guarantees cleanup execution under all conditions.\n- **throw**: Raise custom or built-in exceptions.\n- **Rule**: Never swallow errors; never throw raw strings.",hi:"- **try**: Risk wale code ke liye.\n- **catch**: Galti handle karne ke liye (`name`, `message`, `stack`).\n- **finally**: Har situation mein cleanup run karega.\n- **throw**: Custom exception raise karne ke liye.\n- **Niyam**: Error ko bina log kiye chup na karayein, hamesha `new Error()` throw karein."}}],quiz:[{q:{en:`What will the following function return?

function test() {
  try {
    return 1;
  } finally {
    return 2;
  }
}
console.log(test());`,hi:`Yeh function kya return karega?

function test() {
  try {
    return 1;
  } finally {
    return 2;
  }
}
console.log(test());`},options:[{en:"2",hi:"2"},{en:"1",hi:"1"},{en:"undefined",hi:"undefined"},{en:"SyntaxError",hi:"SyntaxError"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"If a finally block returns a value, that return value overrides any pending return value from the try or catch blocks.",hi:"Agar `finally` block ke andar se koi value return ki jati hai, toh woh `try` ya `catch` ke return value ko override kar deti hai."}},{q:{en:"Which property on an Error object contains the sequence of function calls that led to the exception?",hi:"Error object ki kaunsi property batati hai ki error kis function call sequence aur line number se aayi?"},options:[{en:"error.stack",hi:"error.stack"},{en:"error.message",hi:"error.message"},{en:"error.name",hi:"error.name"},{en:"error.traceback",hi:"error.traceback"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"error.stack provides the stack trace showing the file path, line numbers, and call hierarchy.",hi:"error.stack mein poora call hierarchy, file path aur line number ka trace hota hai."}},{q:{en:"Why is throwing a raw string like `throw 'Network Error'` considered a serious anti-pattern?",hi:"Normal string `throw 'Network Error'` karna ek bad practice kyun maani jaati hai?"},options:[{en:"It lacks a stack trace, making debugging root causes extremely difficult",hi:"Isme stack trace nahi hota, jisse bug ka root cause dhoondhna mushkil ho jata hai"},{en:"It crashes the browser immediately without entering catch",hi:"Yeh catch block mein ghuse bina browser crash kar deta hai"},{en:"JavaScript strictly forbids throwing non-objects",hi:"JavaScript non-objects throw karne ki permission nahi deta"},{en:"It takes 10x more memory than an Error object",hi:"Yeh Error object se 10x zyada memory leta hai"}],answerIndex:0,explanation:{en:"Primitive strings do not capture the call stack or environment metadata at the point of failure.",hi:"Plain string ke paas stack trace aur metadata nahi hota, isliye debugging ke waqt problem ki exact location nahi milti."}},{question:{en:"What is the core architectural purpose of Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors in the modern full-stack MERN ecosystem?",hi:"Modern full-stack MERN ecosystem mein Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ka mukhya architectural maksad kya hota hai?"},options:[{en:"It manages physical computer cooling and power supply",hi:"Ye physical computer cooling aur power supply manage karta hai"},{en:"It provides structured, robust, and scalable patterns for handling error handling: try, catch, finally & custom errors with high performance and maintainability",hi:"Ye high performance aur maintainability ke saath Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ko handle karne ka structured aur scalable pattern provide karta hai"},{en:"It completely replaces JavaScript with binary machine code in browser tabs",hi:"Ye browser tabs mein JavaScript ko binary machine code se replace karta hai"},{en:"It is only used for printing documents to physical printers",hi:"Ye sirf physical printers par documents print karne ke liye hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors establishes clean separation of concerns, ensuring predictable data flow, robust error handling, and optimal runtime performance in production.",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors clean architecture aur separation of concerns deta hai jisse application scalable aur maintainable banti hai."}},{question:{en:"What critical development bottleneck or anti-pattern does Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors directly resolve?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors kis critical development bottleneck ya anti-pattern ko seedhe solve karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It replaces chaotic, tightly coupled ad-hoc logic with declarative, predictable control flow and structured data contracts",hi:"Ye chaotic aur tightly coupled logic ko hata kar declarative, predictable flow aur structured data contracts deta hai"},{en:"It forces the operating system to shut down when errors occur",hi:"Error aane par ye operating system band kar deta hai"},{en:"It deletes all database records older than 24 hours automatically",hi:"Ye 24 ghante purane DB records delete karta hai"},{en:"It blocks all outgoing HTTP network requests to conserve bandwidth",hi:"Ye bandwidth bachane ke liye network requests block karta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Without Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors, applications suffer from brittle code, maintenance overhead, and unhandled edge cases that manifest as production crashes.",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ke bina code brittle ho jata hai aur production mein unexpected errors aate hain."}},{question:{en:"When reasoning about Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors, how is its mental model best conceptualized through real-world analogies?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ko real-world analogies ke zariye kaise best samjha ja sakta hai?"},options:[{en:"As a completely offline computer with zero network or database connections",hi:"Ek offline computer ki tarah jisme koi connection na ho"},{en:"As a disciplined, coordinated workflow where inputs are validated and processed through standardized checkpoints rather than ad-hoc handling",hi:"Ek disciplined workflow ki tarah jahan data ko structured checkpoints ke zariye step-by-step process kiya jata hai"},{en:"As a random number generator with non-deterministic output",hi:"Random number generator ki tarah jiska koi niyam na ho"},{en:"As a static text document that cannot be modified or read",hi:"Static text document jo padha na ja sake"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Real-world workflow analogies help engineers visualize component boundaries, request lifecycles, and data transformations intuitively.",hi:"Real-world analogies component boundaries aur request lifecycle ko visual aur intuitive banati hain."}},{question:{en:"When declaring and implementing Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors, what syntactic convention is essential to prevent runtime errors?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ko declare aur implement karte waqt kaunsa syntax niyam runtime errors rokne ke liye zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Adhering strictly to required parameters, handling asynchronous promises/callbacks cleanly, and verifying return value types",hi:"Zaroori parameters sahi pass karna, async promises ko handle karna aur return value types verify karna"},{en:"Wrapping every line of code inside an eval() execution block",hi:"Har line ko eval() block mein wrap karna"},{en:"Omitting import and require statements to reduce file size",hi:"File size ghatane ke liye import statements hatana"},{en:"Writing all code on a single continuous line without whitespace",hi:"Bina whitespace ke single line par code likhna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Following standard ES6+ syntax contracts and properly handling promise resolution ensures execution safety and eliminates TypeError exceptions.",hi:"ES6+ syntax aur promise handling ke standard rules follow karne se TypeError aur crashes nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"What is a common pitfall developers encounter when working with Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ke saath kaam karte waqt developers aksar kaunsi aam galati karte hain?"},options:[{en:"Writing unit tests before implementing features",hi:"Feature likhne se pehle unit tests likhna"},{en:"Failing to handle failure edge cases, mutating shared state directly, or neglecting defensive validation guard clauses",hi:"Failure edge cases ko handle na karna, shared state direct mutate karna ya validation guard clauses na lagana"},{en:"Using strict equality checks (===) instead of loose equality (==)",hi:"Loose equality ke badle strict equality use karna"},{en:"Writing clear inline code documentation",hi:"Clear inline code comments likhna"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Neglecting edge cases and error handling causes silent regressions and race conditions that surface under concurrent user workloads.",hi:"Edge cases aur error handling miss karne se high-traffic production load mein silent bugs paida hote hain."}},{question:{en:"According to production best practices, how should Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors be architected for enterprise-grade stability?",hi:"Production best practices ke mutabiq enterprise-grade stability ke liye Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ko kaise architect karna chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Enforce modular boundaries, validate all incoming payloads against schemas, log structured context, and maintain pure functions where possible",hi:"Modular boundaries enforce karein, payloads ko schema se validate karein, structured logs rakhein aur pure functions use karein"},{en:"Hardcode sensitive database connection strings directly in client-side files",hi:"Database passwords ko client files mein hardcode karna"},{en:"Disable all linter rules and type warnings globally",hi:"Linter aur type warnings ko globally disable karna"},{en:"Store all user session variables in global un-scoped memory arrays",hi:"Global memory arrays mein sessions store karna"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Enterprise-grade code prioritizes modularity, strict input validation, structured observability, and stateless designs.",hi:"Production hardening ke liye modular code, schema validation aur observability standard rules hote hain."}},{question:{en:"How does proper optimization of Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors impact application memory and CPU consumption?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ko sahi dhang se optimize karne par application memory aur CPU par kya asar padta hai?"},options:[{en:"It increases server CPU temperature to 100 degrees Celsius",hi:"Server CPU temperature 100 degrees kar deta hai"},{en:"It minimizes redundant computations, eliminates memory leaks from uncleaned references, and maintains low latency under high concurrency",hi:"Ye redundant computations ghatata hai, memory leaks khatam karta hai aur high concurrency mein low latency maintain karta hai"},{en:"It doubles heap RAM allocation unconditionally",hi:"Heap RAM ko zabardasti double karta hai"},{en:"Optimization has zero measurable impact in modern web engines",hi:"Modern web engines par optimization ka koi asar nahi hota"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Preventing unnecessary allocations and cleaning up resources ensures low garbage collection pressure and predictable response times.",hi:"Memory leak rokne aur unnecessary allocations hatane se Garbage Collector par load kam rehta hai aur response fast rehta hai."}},{question:{en:"What security principle is non-negotiable when handling data within Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors mein data handle karte waqt kaunsa security principle non-negotiable hota hai?"},options:[{en:"Never trust client-supplied input: always sanitize, authenticate, authorize, and validate against strict schemas on the server",hi:"Client data par blind trust na karein: server par hamesha sanitize, authenticate, authorize aur validate karein"},{en:"Trust all requests coming from mobile devices or web browsers blindly",hi:"Mobile ya browser se aane wali requests par blind trust karein"},{en:"Disable HTTPS and SSL certificates to maximize raw network throughput",hi:"Network throughput ke liye HTTPS band karein"},{en:"Expose database admin credentials to all registered users",hi:"Database admin credentials sabhi users ko expose karein"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Zero-Trust security dictates that every incoming request and data mutation must be validated and authenticated server-side before processing.",hi:"Zero-Trust security ke mutabiq har incoming mutation ko server par strictly validate aur authenticate kiya jana chahiye."}},{question:{en:"How does asynchronous non-blocking execution operate in Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors mein asynchronous non-blocking execution kaise kaam karta hai?"},options:[{en:"It freezes the entire operating system until each operation completes",hi:"Har operation complete hone tak operating system freeze rehta hai"},{en:"I/O operations return Promises or accept callbacks, delegating work to background threads/queues while the main thread remains free to handle incoming tasks",hi:"I/O operations Promises return karte hain aur background queues use karke main thread ko baaki requests ke liye free rakhte hain"},{en:"Async operations execute in reverse alphabetical order automatically",hi:"Async operations reverse alphabetical order mein chalte hain"},{en:"Async code only executes when triggered manually by a user click",hi:"Sirf manual user click par async code chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Non-blocking asynchronous operations resolve via microtasks or event loop queues, ensuring the runtime thread serves concurrent requests smoothly.",hi:"Non-blocking model main thread ko free rakhta hai taaki server bina rukaawat ke multiple users ko simultaneously serve kar sake."}},{question:{en:"What is the recommended pattern for propagating errors that occur in Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors mein error aane par unhe propagate karne ka recommended pattern kya hai?"},options:[{en:"Intercepting the error, enriching it with operational context, and delegating to a centralized error handler or error boundary",hi:"Error ko intercept karna, debug context add karna, aur centralized error handler ya error boundary ko pass karna"},{en:"Swallowing errors silently with empty catch {} blocks to hide problems from logs",hi:"Khaali catch {} blocks se errors ko silently daba dena taaki logs mein na dikhein"},{en:"Shutting down the server machine power immediately",hi:"Server machine power turant band kar dena"},{en:"Sending internal raw stack traces and database credentials to end-user browsers",hi:"Raw stack trace aur DB passwords browser par bhej dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Centralized error propagation provides complete operational observability while shielding internal infrastructure details from end users.",hi:"Centralized error handling se system mein transparency rehti hai aur user ko clean, safe error messages milte hain."}},{question:{en:"When authoring unit or integration tests for Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors, what must the test suite assert?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ke liye automated tests likhte waqt test suite ko kya assert karna zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Only that the JavaScript file can be saved to disk",hi:"Sirf ye ki file disk par save ho sake"},{en:"Both the happy path (expected inputs producing valid outputs) AND boundary edge cases (null, empty arrays, network timeouts, invalid types)",hi:"Happy path (valid data) AUR boundary edge cases (null, empty array, network timeout, invalid types) dono ko verify karna"},{en:"That the test suite takes at least 24 hours to finish running",hi:"Test suite ko 24 ghante chalna chahiye"},{en:"Testing is considered unnecessary in modern full-stack development",hi:"Modern development mein testing zaroori nahi hai"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Robust automated test suites verify both standard valid scenarios and defensive failure modes to prevent regressions during deployments.",hi:"Achhi testing valid inputs aur failure states dono ko assert karti hai taaki production deployments safe rahein."}},{question:{en:"How does modular design enhance code maintainability in Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors?",hi:"Modular design Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors mein code maintainability ko kaise badhata hai?"},options:[{en:"By isolating distinct responsibilities into small, reusable, and independently testable units following the Single Responsibility Principle",hi:"Single Responsibility Principle ke zariye alag-alag kaamo ko chote, reusable aur testable units mein baant kar"},{en:"By combining all frontend, backend, and database code into a single 50,000-line script",hi:"Saara code ek hi 50,000-line script mein daal kar"},{en:"By removing all function names and replacing them with random numbers",hi:"Function names hata kar random numbers likhna"},{en:"By forbidding code comments and documentation across the repository",hi:"Comments aur documentation ban kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Modularity reduces cognitive load, simplifies debugging, prevents ripple effects during changes, and enables seamless team collaboration.",hi:"Modular code se readability badhti hai, debugging aasan hoti hai aur ek jagah badlav karne par doosri jagah bugs nahi aate."}},{question:{en:"When application traffic scales 100x, how should Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors be architected to support horizontal scaling?",hi:"Traffic 100x badhne par Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ko horizontally scale karne ke liye kya design approach honi chahiye?"},options:[{en:"Ensure the component/service is completely stateless, offload shared session/state to Redis/MongoDB, and distribute traffic via a load balancer",hi:"Service ko completely stateless banayein, shared state ko Redis/DB par shift karein aur load balancer se traffic distribute karein"},{en:"Store all user session variables in local in-memory JavaScript objects on the web server",hi:"Server ki local RAM mein session variables store karna"},{en:"Reboot the production server manually whenever memory usage exceeds 10%",hi:"Memory 10% cross hote hi server manually reboot karna"},{en:"Block 95% of incoming users using firewall rules",hi:"95% users ko firewall se block kar dena"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Stateless service architecture guarantees that any container instance can handle any incoming request, enabling dynamic auto-scaling without session loss.",hi:"Stateless architecture auto-scaling ka base hai jahan naye containers bina session loss ke instant traffic handle kar sakte hain."}},{question:{en:"In the full-stack MERN paradigm, where does Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors properly belong and execute?",hi:"Full-stack MERN architecture mein Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors kahan belong karta hai aur kahan execute hota hai?"},options:[{en:"In its designated architectural tier (Client browser UI, Express API backend, or MongoDB database) with clean API contracts connecting them",hi:"Apne designated tier (Browser UI, Express API backend, ya MongoDB) mein clean API contracts ke saath"},{en:"Directly on the end-user's local router firmware",hi:"User ke local router firmware par"},{en:"Inside the computer motherboard BIOS chip",hi:"Motherboard BIOS chip mein"},{en:"All MERN code runs strictly inside the MongoDB database engine",hi:"Saara MERN code sirf MongoDB ke andar chalta hai"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Maintaining clear structural boundaries between client rendering, backend orchestration, and database persistence is the defining trait of MERN.",hi:"Client UI, backend server aur database ke beech saaf boundary maintain karna MERN architecture ka mukhya niyam hai."}},{question:{en:"What telemetry metric or observability signal is most crucial for diagnosing issues with Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors in production?",hi:"Production mein Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ki problems diagnose karne ke liye sabse zaroori telemetry metric kaunsi hoti hai?"},options:[{en:"The desktop monitor brightness setting of the client",hi:"Client ke monitor ki brightness"},{en:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (HTTP 4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), and heap memory allocation deltas",hi:"Latency percentiles (p95/p99), error rates (4xx/5xx), throughput (RPS), aur heap memory allocation deltas"},{en:"The number of files in the project's root folder",hi:"Root folder mein files ki sankhya"},{en:"The physical keyboard model used by the engineer",hi:"Engineer ke keyboard ka model"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Observability platforms monitor p95/p99 latencies, error frequencies, and memory utilization to identify bottlenecks and regressions early.",hi:"p95/p99 latencies aur error rates monitor karne se crashes aane se pehle hi bottlenecks pakad mein aa jaate hain."}},{question:{en:"Why is eliminating unintended side effects essential when authoring logic for Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors ka logic likhte waqt unintended side effects ko khatam karna kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"Side effects introduce unpredictability, corrupt shared state, cause race conditions, and make concurrent code nearly impossible to debug",hi:"Side effects se code unpredictable banta hai, shared state corrupt hoti hai aur race conditions create hoti hain"},{en:"Side effects permanently erase the developer's Git commit history",hi:"Git history permanently delete ho jaati hai"},{en:"Side effects are strictly required by the JavaScript ECMAScript standard",hi:"ECMAScript mein side effects required hain"},{en:"Side effects make all algorithms execute in O(1) time",hi:"Saare algorithms O(1) time mein chalte hain"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Pure and predictable logic produces the same output for identical inputs, guaranteeing thread safety, easy caching, and high reliability.",hi:"Pure logic se shared state safe rehti hai aur same input par hamesha consistent aur predictable output milta hai."}},{question:{en:"How should client-side state be kept in sync with backend server mutations in Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors mein client-side state aur backend server data ko sync mein kaise rakha jata hai?"},options:[{en:"By forcing a complete hard page refresh every 3 seconds",hi:"Har 3 second mein poora page hard refresh karke"},{en:"Using optimistic UI updates with error rollback, automated query cache invalidation (TanStack Query/RTK), or WebSocket change streams",hi:"Optimistic UI updates with rollback, automated query cache invalidation ya WebSocket push streams use karke"},{en:"By disabling all database update operations permanently",hi:"Database updates ko permanently band karke"},{en:"By saving user state in local CSV files on the server desktop",hi:"Server desktop par CSV files save karke"}],correctAnswer:1,explanation:{en:"Modern full-stack architectures synchronize state seamlessly using query cache invalidation, optimistic updates, and real-time socket events.",hi:"Modern apps cache invalidation aur optimistic UI use karti hain taaki UI bina screen reload ke instantly updated rahe."}},{question:{en:"Why is thorough resource cleanup (clearing timers, closing sockets, aborting in-flight requests) critical in Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors?",hi:"Error Handling: try, catch, finally & Custom Errors mein resource cleanup (timers clear karna, sockets band karna, network abort karna) kyun zaroori hai?"},options:[{en:"To prevent memory leaks where unreachable or orphaned objects remain retained in heap memory, causing gradual performance degradation and crashes",hi:"Memory leaks rokne ke liye taaki unneeded objects RAM mein jama na hon aur server crash na ho"},{en:"To delete the client's local disk partition",hi:"Client ka local disk partition delete karne ke liye"},{en:"Because JavaScript engines allow only 5 variables in RAM",hi:"JS engine sirf 5 variables allow karta hai"},{en:"Cleanup is unnecessary because garbage collection handles 100% of event listeners automatically",hi:"Cleanup ki zaroorat nahi hoti"}],correctAnswer:0,explanation:{en:"Unclosed connections and dangling event listeners create references that prevent garbage collection, leading to severe memory leaks over time.",hi:"Dangling listeners aur unclosed connections memory leaks banate hain jo V8 heap ko exhaust karke process crash kar dete hain."}}]};export{e as default};
